1
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:08,457
早上好，我是鲸鱼娘，今天是10月4日。
Good morning, I'm Whale Girl. Today is October 4.

2
00:00:08,477 --> 00:00:12,168
今天说七件事：苹果收紧 Mac 的完全磁盘权限，
Seven stories today: Apple tightens Full Disk Access on Mac,

3
00:00:12,188 --> 00:00:14,968
Antigravity 用上 Claude 5.5，
Antigravity gets Claude 5.5,

4
00:00:14,988 --> 00:00:18,948
Gemini 加了地图工具，Meta 开源 Muse 硬件，
Gemini adds a Map tool, Meta open-sources Muse hardware,

5
00:00:18,968 --> 00:00:23,268
Suno 能做有声配乐了，Supabase 融资收购 Turso，
Suno now makes speech with music, Supabase raises money and buys Turso,

6
00:00:23,288 --> 00:00:27,225
还有一位物理学家用 Claude 写了 36 篇论文。
and a physicist wrote 36 papers with Claude.

7
00:00:27,245 --> 00:00:31,435
第一件，10 月 2 日，苹果在开发者网站上发了一条公告，
First, on October 2, Apple posted a notice on its developer site

8
00:00:31,455 --> 00:00:34,674
说要收紧 Mac 上的“完全磁盘访问”权限。
saying it will tighten Full Disk Access on the Mac.

9
00:00:34,694 --> 00:00:38,160
这个权限本来是给备份软件用的，开了以后，
This permission exists so backup apps can work, and once it's on,

10
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:41,000
应用能绕过系统的大部分隐私保护。
an app can sidestep most of the system's privacy controls.

11
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:43,345
苹果说，有些开发者在滥用它，
Apple says some developers misuse it,

12
00:00:43,365 --> 00:00:47,755
能看到你的文件、邮件、信息，甚至浏览记录。
exposing your files, mail, messages and even browsing history.

13
00:00:47,775 --> 00:00:52,790
以后用户想给某个应用开这个权限，要做非常明确的操作才行。
Going forward, users will need to take a very explicit action to grant an app this access.

14
00:00:52,810 --> 00:00:56,759
苹果还专门提到：AI 智能体越来越能干、越来越自主，
Apple also noted that as AI agents become more capable and autonomous,

15
00:00:56,779 --> 00:00:59,501
开这种权限的风险会大大增加。
the risk of this level of access will grow substantially.

16
00:00:59,521 --> 00:01:03,186
IT之家报道说，macOS 27 等系统都会跟进，
IT Home reports that macOS 27 and other systems will follow,

17
00:01:03,206 --> 00:01:05,787
但苹果还没说哪天上线。
but Apple hasn't said when it will ship.

18
00:01:05,807 --> 00:01:08,602
如果你在 Mac 上用会读写文件的 AI 工具，
If you use AI tools that read and write files on a Mac,

19
00:01:08,622 --> 00:01:11,441
到时候授权可能会多几步。
granting access may take a few more steps.

20
00:01:11,641 --> 00:01:14,446
第二件，谷歌的 AI 编程工具 Antigravity，
Second, Google's AI coding tool Antigravity

21
00:01:14,466 --> 00:01:19,186
模型列表里加上了 Claude Opus 5.5 和 Claude Sonnet 5.5。
added Claude Opus 5.5 and Claude Sonnet 5.5 to its model list.

22
00:01:19,206 --> 00:01:23,076
Let's Data Science 在 10 月 3 日报道了这次更新，
Let's Data Science reported the update on October 3.

23
00:01:23,096 --> 00:01:25,313
两个都是带思考的版本。
Both are thinking versions.

24
00:01:25,333 --> 00:01:29,549
不过只有 Google AI Pro 和 Google AI Ultra 的付费用户能选。
But only paying Google AI Pro and Google AI Ultra subscribers can pick them.

25
00:01:29,569 --> 00:01:32,099
Pro 还得是正式订阅，试用的不行；
Pro must be a non-trial subscription; trials don't count.

26
00:01:32,119 --> 00:01:35,277
免费版、AI Plus 和企业版也都不在名单里。
Free, AI Plus and Enterprise accounts aren't on the list either.

27
00:01:35,297 --> 00:01:38,562
同时，旧的 Claude Opus 4.6、Claude Sonnet 4.6，
Meanwhile, the older Claude Opus 4.6, Claude Sonnet 4.6

28
00:01:38,582 --> 00:01:44,302
还有 GPT-OSS-120B，会在 11 月 2 日从 Antigravity 下架。
and GPT-OSS-120B will leave Antigravity on November 2.

29
00:01:44,322 --> 00:01:47,730
谷歌自家的 Gemini 模型照常对所有套餐开放。
Google's own Gemini models stay open to every plan.

30
00:01:47,750 --> 00:01:51,401
所以免费用户之后在 Antigravity 里就用不到 Claude 了，
So free users will lose Claude in Antigravity,

31
00:01:51,421 --> 00:01:53,633
想用得开付费订阅。
and will need a paid plan to keep using it.

32
00:01:53,833 --> 00:01:56,554
第三件，10 月 2 日，9to5Google 发现，
Third, on October 2, 9to5Google spotted

33
00:01:56,574 --> 00:02:01,232
Gemini 手机应用多了一个 Map 地图工具，安卓和 iOS 都有。
a new Map tool in the Gemini mobile app, on both Android and iOS.

34
00:02:01,252 --> 00:02:03,612
它在输入框旁边那排工具的最后，
It sits at the end of the tool carousel,

35
00:02:03,632 --> 00:02:06,732
和照片、相机、文件、云端硬盘放在一起。
next to Photos, Camera, Files and Drive.

36
00:02:06,752 --> 00:02:10,177
点开是你当前位置的实时地图，中间有个圆圈，
It opens a live map of where you are, with a circle in the middle.

37
00:02:10,197 --> 00:02:12,897
可以拖动、缩放，也能搜别的地方。
You can pan, zoom, or search other places.

38
00:02:12,917 --> 00:02:15,388
选好以后，输入框里会多一个“地图区域”，
Once you pick a spot, a Map Area chip is added to the prompt box,

39
00:02:15,408 --> 00:02:17,298
你再打字问这一带的事。
and you type your question about that area.

40
00:02:17,318 --> 00:02:20,746
这个工具已经大范围推送了，但网页版没有。
The tool is widely rolled out, but not on the web.

41
00:02:20,766 --> 00:02:22,796
另外，谷歌应用 17.63 测试版里，
Also, in Google app beta 17.63,

42
00:02:22,816 --> 00:02:25,256
调用技能的符号从斜杠换成了 @，
the symbol for skills changes from a slash to @,

43
00:02:25,276 --> 00:02:29,772
和连接的应用放在一起，这个还没全面推开。
alongside connected apps. That isn't widely rolled out yet.

44
00:02:29,972 --> 00:02:33,587
第四件，10 月 2 日，Meta 发布了 Muse Gadgets，
Fourth, on October 2, Meta announced Muse Gadgets,

45
00:02:33,607 --> 00:02:36,658
让大家自己动手做能接上 Muse 的硬件。
so anyone can build their own hardware that works with Muse.

46
00:02:36,678 --> 00:02:39,278
Muse 是 Meta 上个月推出的 AI 智能体。
Muse is the AI agent Meta launched last month.

47
00:02:39,298 --> 00:02:44,730
这次开源了一套 ESP32 开发板用的固件，和一套 Linux SDK。
Meta open-sourced firmware for ESP32 boards and a Linux SDK.

48
00:02:44,750 --> 00:02:48,560
也就是说，用便宜的 ESP32 板子或者树莓派，
So with a cheap ESP32 board or a Raspberry Pi,

49
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:50,780
接上屏幕、按钮、传感器，
plus a screen, buttons and sensors,

50
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:52,932
就能做一个 Muse 小设备。
you can build a small Muse device.

51
00:02:52,952 --> 00:02:55,432
Meta 自己也做了一个：Muse Home Link，
Meta also made its own: Muse Home Link,

52
00:02:55,452 --> 00:03:00,511
插 USB-C 供电，让 Muse 连上家里的电视、音箱这些设备。
a USB-C powered device that lets Muse reach your TV, speakers and other devices at home.

53
00:03:00,531 --> 00:03:01,621
TechCrunch 说，
TechCrunch says

54
00:03:01,641 --> 00:03:04,581
这是 Meta 超级智能实验室的产品负责人
Meta Superintelligence Labs' head of product,

55
00:03:04,601 --> 00:03:07,346
Nat Friedman 在 X 上宣布的。
Nat Friedman, announced it on X.

56
00:03:07,366 --> 00:03:09,366
它一共做了 5000 台，
Meta made 5,000 units.

57
00:03:09,386 --> 00:03:13,942
Muse 订阅用户可以免费申请一台，数量有限，几周内发货。
Muse subscribers can request one for free while supplies last, shipping within weeks.

58
00:03:13,962 --> 00:03:17,609
这套代码已经开源，用的是 Apache 2.0 许可。
The code is open source under the Apache 2.0 license.

59
00:03:17,629 --> 00:03:19,370
Home Link 只给 Muse 订阅用户，
Home Link is only for Muse subscribers,

60
00:03:19,390 --> 00:03:22,355
国内用户可以先看看开源代码。
so users in China can check out the open-source code for now.

61
00:03:22,555 --> 00:03:24,020
第五件，10 月 1 日，
Fifth, on October 1,

62
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:28,008
做 AI 音乐的 Suno 推出了 Speech，现在是测试版。
AI music company Suno launched Speech, now in beta.

63
00:03:28,028 --> 00:03:32,399
它能把说话的声音和背景音乐，当成一条完整的音轨一起生成。
It generates the spoken voice and the background music together as one cohesive track.

64
00:03:32,419 --> 00:03:36,610
以前常见的做法是先合成语音，再另外配一段音乐。
The usual way was to make the voice first, then add music separately.

65
00:03:36,630 --> 00:03:41,010
用法很简单：输入一段想法、一首诗或者你写的文字，
Using it is simple: type an idea, a poem or something you wrote,

66
00:03:41,030 --> 00:03:43,735
再描述想要的声音和音乐风格。
then describe the voice and music style you want.

67
00:03:43,755 --> 00:03:48,056
官方举的例子有冥想、诗、打气的话和睡前故事。
Suno's examples include meditations, poems, pep talks and bedtime stories.

68
00:03:48,076 --> 00:03:51,301
Suno 说，过去一个月先给一小批人试了，
Suno says a small group tested it over the past month,

69
00:03:51,321 --> 00:03:53,824
现在向所有人开放测试版。
and the beta is now open to everyone.

70
00:03:53,844 --> 00:03:58,130
官方也承认有毛病，比如英国口音有时会跑成澳大利亚口音，
Suno admits there are issues: British accents can drift to Australian,

71
00:03:58,150 --> 00:04:00,410
停顿也可能太夸张。
and pauses can get too dramatic.

72
00:04:00,610 --> 00:04:04,836
第六件，10 月 2 日，开源数据库平台 Supabase
Sixth, on October 2, open-source database platform Supabase

73
00:04:04,856 --> 00:04:06,736
宣布拿到 1.5 亿美元新融资，
announced $150 million in new funding,

74
00:04:06,756 --> 00:04:09,081
由新加坡的 GIC 领投。
led by Singapore's GIC.

75
00:04:09,101 --> 00:04:12,694
距离它上一轮 5 亿美元的 F 轮，才过了四个月。
That's just four months after its $500 million Series F.

76
00:04:12,714 --> 00:04:13,925
同时它要收购 Turso。
It's also acquiring Turso.

77
00:04:13,945 --> 00:04:16,745
Turso 用 Rust 重写了 SQLite，
Turso rebuilt SQLite in Rust,

78
00:04:16,765 --> 00:04:19,903
一台服务器就能管几百万个数据库。
and one server can manage millions of databases.

79
00:04:19,923 --> 00:04:20,667
为什么要买？
Why buy it?

80
00:04:20,687 --> 00:04:25,043
Supabase 说，现在每月新建 400 万个数据库，
Supabase says 4 million new databases are created each month,

81
00:04:25,063 --> 00:04:28,033
其中 70% 是智能体或 AI 工具建的。
and 70% are made by agents or AI tools.

82
00:04:28,053 --> 00:04:30,255
智能体要随手开一个小数据库，
Agents want to spin up small databases on demand

83
00:04:30,275 --> 00:04:33,317
用完就停，Turso 正好适合这种用法。
and suspend them after use, and Turso fits that well.

84
00:04:33,337 --> 00:04:36,502
这笔钱会用在员工套现和智能体新功能上，
The money will go to employee liquidity and new agent features,

85
00:04:36,522 --> 00:04:38,762
比如新出的 Supabase Compute，
like the new Supabase Compute,

86
00:04:38,782 --> 00:04:42,582
给长时间运行的智能体提供托管沙箱。
which offers hosted sandboxes for long-running agents.

87
00:04:42,602 --> 00:04:46,943
收购价格没有公布，Turso 的两位创始人会加入 Supabase。
The price wasn't disclosed. Turso's two founders will join Supabase.

88
00:04:46,963 --> 00:04:49,258
官方说，Turso 的老用户一切照旧，
The company says nothing changes for existing Turso users,

89
00:04:49,278 --> 00:04:51,474
产品继续做下去。
and the product will keep going.

90
00:04:51,674 --> 00:04:55,154
最后一件，The Decoder 10 月 3 日报道，
Last one: The Decoder reported on October 3

91
00:04:55,174 --> 00:04:57,134
哈佛物理学家 Matthew Schwartz
that Harvard physicist Matthew Schwartz

92
00:04:57,154 --> 00:05:00,054
用开源工具 BootLoops 加上 Claude，
used the open-source tool BootLoops with Claude

93
00:05:00,074 --> 00:05:01,877
三个月写了 36 篇论文。
to write 36 papers in three months.

94
00:05:01,897 --> 00:05:03,517
这些论文跨了 18 个领域，
The papers span 18 fields,

95
00:05:03,537 --> 00:05:07,769
从粒子物理到语言学都有，一共 19 位合作者。
from particle physics to linguistics, with 19 co-authors.

96
00:05:07,789 --> 00:05:11,490
BootLoops 是一套帮大模型做精确科学计算的工具，
BootLoops is a toolkit that helps language models do precise scientific calculations.

97
00:05:11,510 --> 00:05:15,772
代码开源，经费来自 Anthropic，但它不是 Anthropic 的项目。
It's open source and funded by Anthropic, but it's not an Anthropic project.

98
00:05:15,792 --> 00:05:17,548
成果里有 30 个粒子物理积分，
The results include 30 particle physics integrals:

99
00:05:17,568 --> 00:05:20,871
一半是重算已知结果，另一半是新的。
15 reproduce known results and 15 are new.

100
00:05:20,891 --> 00:05:24,329
还做了一个覆盖 6072 种语言的重音数据库。
It also built a word stress database covering 6,072 languages.

101
00:05:24,349 --> 00:05:27,714
不过 Schwartz 自己提醒，Claude 经常太早宣布成功，
But Schwartz warns that Claude often declares victory too early,

102
00:05:27,734 --> 00:05:30,246
算对了也可能得出错的结论。
and can draw wrong conclusions even when the math is right.

103
00:05:30,266 --> 00:05:34,493
所以结果还得有懂行的人来检查，AI 只是帮手。
So the results still need checking by experts. AI is just a helper.

104
00:05:34,693 --> 00:05:37,323
今天就这些，来源都在简介里。
That's all for today. Sources are in the description.

105
00:05:37,343 --> 00:05:39,023
国庆假期还剩几天，
There are a few days left in the National Day holiday.

106
00:05:39,043 --> 00:05:41,505
好好休息，我们明天见。
Get some rest, and see you tomorrow.
